{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BpDXMwv3zxyLVTE5Be6t3Z","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive understanding. Let me create the final report:\n\n## Comprehensive Round 0 Evaluation Architecture Report\n\nBased on a thorough investigation of `/home/georg/stark-backend`, here is the complete per-AIR Round 0 evaluation flow and infrastructure details:\n\n---\n\n### **1. CURRENT PER-AIR PROCESSING PIPELINE (sumcheck_uni_round0_polys)**\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\n#### **Phase 1: Work Item Preparation (Lines 1022-1152)**\n- **Lines 1024-1109**: Build per-AIR work items via `Round0AirWorkItem<HS>` struct (line 212)\n- **Lines 1042-1082**: Pre-compute buffer size capacities per AIR using unsafe CUDA functions:\n  - `_zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size()` (line 1045)\n  - `_zerocheck_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size()` (line 1054)\n  - `_logup_r0_intermediates_buffer_size()` (line 1067)\n  - `_logup_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size()` (line 1076)\n- **Lines 1111-1122**: Sort work items by descending height for load balance\n- **Lines 1114-1122**: Pre-compute extraction transform matrices per unique constraint degree (cached in `FxHashMap<usize, Round0ExtractTables>`)\n- **Lines 1127-1152**: Pre-allocate device batch polynomial array (`d_batch_array`) - all results written here per-AIR by GPU extraction kernels\n\n#### **Phase 2: Multi-Stream Dispatch (Lines 1204-1420)**\n- **Lines 1208-1226**: Dynamic thread count decision based on AIR count and memory budget\n- **Lines 1229-1273**: Pre-allocate per-thread buffers using **95th percentile threshold** (line 1185):\n  ```rust\n  let percentile_idx = |n: usize| -> usize { (n * 95 / 100).min(n.saturating_sub(1)) };\n  ```\n  Creates `Round0ThreadBuffers` with:\n  - `zc_intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>`\n  - `zc_temp_sums: DeviceBuffer<EF>`\n  - `logup_intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>`\n  - `logup_temp_sums: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>`\n\n- **Lines 1280-1318**: Single-threaded path (num_threads ≤ 1):\n  1. Upload `d_eq_3b_per_trace` sequentially\n  2. Precompute logup combinations\n  3. Process all AIRs sequentially calling `process_air_round0()`\n\n- **Lines 1319-1420**: Multi-threaded path (num_threads > 1):\n  1. **Lines 1320-1330**: Round-robin work distribution across threads for load balance\n  2. **Lines 1341-1382**: Background precompute thread spawned to overlap:\n     - Upload `d_eq_3b_per_trace`\n     - Precompute logup combinations\n     - All on background thread's `cudaStreamPerThread`\n  3. **Lines 1385-1406**: Round 0 worker threads spawned for each thread buffer:\n     - Process assigned AIR work items sequentially\n     - Call `process_air_round0()` per AIR\n     - Sync worker streams before exit (line 1401)\n\n#### **Phase 3: Results Collection (Lines 1422-1447)**\n- **Lines 1423-1427**: Single D2H copy of entire `d_batch_array`\n- **Lines 1428-1444**: Reconstruct per-AIR `UnivariatePoly` from batch array using precomputed `poly_lens`\n\n---\n\n### **2. PROCESS_AIR_ROUND0 FUNCTION (Lines 244-389)**\n\nThis is the core per-AIR kernel orchestration function:\n\n**Call sequence:**\n1. **Zerocheck Phase (Lines 291-326)**:\n   - Calls `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu()` (line 291)\n   - Launches `zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints` CUDA kernel\n   - If results exist, calls GPU extraction kernel `_round0_extract_zerocheck_poly()` (line 314)\n   - Writes to batch array at offset `w.zc_batch_offset`\n\n2. **Logup Phase (Lines 328-386)**:\n   - Calls `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()` (line 346)\n   - Launches `logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0` CUDA kernel\n   - If results exist, calls GPU extraction kernel `_round0_extract_logup_polys()` (line 373)\n   - Writes numerator to `w.numer_batch_offset`, denominator to `w.denom_batch_offset`\n\n---\n\n### **3. CUDA KERNEL SIGNATURES**\n\n#### **Zerocheck Kernel** (`zerocheck_round0.cu`, Line 148-166)\n```cuda\ntemplate <uint32_t NUM_COSETS, bool GLOBAL, bool NEEDS_SHMEM>\n__global__ void zerocheck_ntt_evaluate_constraints_kernel(\n    FpExt *__restrict__ tmp_sums_buffer,     // [num_blocks][NUM_COSETS][skip_domain]\n    const Fp *__restrict__ selectors_cube,   // [3][num_x]\n    const Fp *__restrict__ preprocessed,\n    const Fp *const *__restrict__ main_parts,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ eq_cube,       // [num_x]\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ d_lambda_pows,\n    const Fp *__restrict__ public_values,\n    const Rule *__restrict__ d_rules,\n    size_t rules_len,\n    const size_t *__restrict__ d_used_nodes,\n    size_t used_nodes_len,\n    size_t lambda_len,\n    uint32_t buffer_size,\n    Fp *__restrict__ d_intermediates,        // Per-AIR intermediates buffer\n    uint32_t skip_domain,\n    uint32_t num_x,\n    uint32_t height,\n    Fp g_shift                               // Coset shift generator\n)\n```\n\nPer-AIR parameters:\n- `skip_domain`: 2^l_skip (evaluation domain size)\n- `num_x`: 2^n_lift (trace height in lifted domain)\n- `num_cosets`: constraint_degree - 1 (for zerocheck quotient)\n- `g_shift`: Two-adic generator for coset shifts\n\n#### **Logup Kernel** (`logup_round0.cu`, Line 161-178)\n```cuda\ntemplate <uint32_t NUM_COSETS, bool GLOBAL, bool NEEDS_SHMEM>\n__global__ void logup_r0_ntt_eval_interactions_kernel(\n    FracExt *__restrict__ tmp_sums_buffer,   // [NUM_COSETS][gridDim.x][skip_domain]\n    const Fp *__restrict__ selectors_cube,   // [3][num_x]\n    const Fp *__restrict__ preprocessed,\n    const Fp *const *__restrict__ main_parts,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ eq_cube,       // [num_x]\n    const Fp *__restrict__ public_values,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ numer_weights, // Per-interaction weights for count expressions\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ denom_weights, // Per-interaction weights for message expressions\n    FpExt denom_sum_init,                    // sum(eq_3bs[i] * beta[msg_len_i] * (bus_i+1))\n    const Rule *__restrict__ d_rules,\n    size_t rules_len,\n    uint32_t buffer_size,\n    Fp *__restrict__ d_intermediates,        // Per-AIR intermediates buffer\n    uint32_t skip_domain,\n    uint32_t num_x,\n    uint32_t height,\n    Fp g_shift\n)\n```\n\nPer-AIR parameters:\n- Same as zerocheck, plus:\n- `numer_weights/denom_weights`: Pre-weighted constraint node indices per interaction\n- `denom_sum_init`: Initial denominator accumulation value\n\n#### **Extraction Kernels** (`round0_extract.cu`)\n```cuda\n// Zerocheck: map evaluation values to polynomial coefficients (with adjustment)\nextern \"C\" int _round0_extract_zerocheck_poly(\n    FpExt* d_out,           // Per-AIR output polynomial\n    const FpExt* d_evals,   // Evaluation results from kernel\n    const FpExt* d_transform,  // Pre-computed transformation matrix\n    uint32_t input_size,    // (constraint_degree-1) * skip_domain\n    uint32_t output_size    // sumcheck_round0_deg(l_skip, constraint_degree) + 1\n)\n\n// Logup: unpacks FracExt, applies norm_factor, extracts numer/denom\nextern \"C\" int _round0_extract_logup_polys(\n    FpExt* d_out_numer,\n    FpExt* d_out_denom,\n    const FracExt* d_evals,\n    const FpExt* d_transform,\n    uint32_t input_size,    // constraint_degree * skip_domain\n    uint32_t output_size,   // constraint_degree * skip_domain\n    FpExt norm_factor       // Accounts for n_lift scaling\n)\n```\n\n---\n\n### **4. NTT COSET EVALUATION INSIDE KERNELS**\n\nThe kernels evaluate constraints/interactions on multiple cosets simultaneously:\n\n**Evaluation Context** (`NttEvalContext<NUM_COSETS>`):\n- Initialized per x_int iteration (logup_round0.cu, Lines 249-261)\n- Contains:\n  - `inter_buffer`: Intermediates storage (either local array or global memory)\n  - `ntt_buffer`: Shared memory or local for NTT operations\n  - `omega_shifts[NUM_COSETS]`: Coset shift points (identity=1, rest=g^c for coset c)\n  - `buffer_stride`: Layout stride in global intermediates buffer\n\n**Per-coset computation**:\n1. **Lines 263-269**: Compute coset shifts:\n   ```cuda\n   eval_ctx.omega_shifts[0] = Fp::one();      // Identity coset\n   g_coset = g_shift;\n   for (c = 1; c < NUM_COSETS; c++) {\n       eval_ctx.omega_shifts[c] = pow(g_coset, ntt_idx_rev);\n       g_coset *= g_shift;\n   }\n   ```\n\n2. **Lines 272-295**: For each x_int value:\n   - Compute per-coset selectors (is_first[c], is_last[c])\n   - Call `acc_interactions<NUM_COSETS>()` (line 284) which evaluates all cosets lockstep\n   - Weight results by eq_cube[x_int]\n\n3. **Intermediates storage** (zerocheck_round0.cu Lines 113-123):\n   - If `header.buffer_result && buffer_size > 0`:\n   ```cuda\n   // Layout: [buffer_size][NUM_COSETS] per thread\n   eval_ctx.inter_buffer[z_index * buffer_stride + c] = x_vals[c];\n   ```\n\n---\n\n### **5. INTERMEDIATES BUFFER SIZE COMPUTATION**\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/eval_config.cuh`\n\n#### **Formula for Zerocheck Intermediates (Lines 84-106)**\n```cpp\ninline uint32_t intermediates_buffer_size(\n    uint32_t buffer_size,      // Number of intermediate nodes in DAG\n    uint32_t skip_domain,\n    uint32_t num_x,\n    uint32_t num_cosets,\n    size_t max_temp_bytes,\n    uint32_t buffer_threshold,\n    uint32_t threads_per_block\n) {\n    if (buffer_size <= buffer_threshold) {\n        return 0;  // Uses only shared/local memory\n    }\n    auto [grid, block] = eval_constraints_launch_params(...);\n    // Layout: [buffer_size][num_threads][num_cosets]\n    return grid.x * block.x * buffer_size * num_cosets;  // Line 106\n}\n```\n\n**Key factors per AIR:**\n- `buffer_size`: Count of intermediate nodes in constraint DAG (u32 field)\n- `num_x`: 2^n_lift (trace height in lifted domain)\n- `num_cosets`: constraint_degree - 1 (zerocheck), constraint_degree (logup)\n- `skip_domain`: 2^l_skip (evaluates constraint_degree many polynomial shifts)\n\n**Pre-computed at keygen:**\n- `zerocheck_round0.inner.buffer_size` stored in `SymbolicRulesGpu::buffer_size` (line 64, round0.rs)\n- `logup_round0_buffer_size` stored in `GpuDeviceStarkProvingKeyOtherData` (pkey.rs, line 35)\n\n#### **Formula for Zerocheck Temp Sums (Lines 61-80)**\n```cpp\ninline uint32_t temp_sums_buffer_size(\n    uint32_t buffer_size,\n    uint32_t skip_domain,\n    uint32_t num_x,\n    uint32_t num_cosets,\n    size_t max_temp_bytes,\n    uint32_t buffer_threshold,\n    uint32_t threads_per_block\n) {\n    auto [grid, _] = eval_constraints_launch_params(...);\n    // Output layout: [num_blocks][num_cosets * skip_domain]\n    return grid.x * num_cosets * skip_domain;  // Line 80\n}\n```\n\n**Per-AIR computation in Rust** (mod.rs Lines 1042-1082):\n```rust\nlet zc_buffer_size = single_pk.other_data.zerocheck_round0.inner.buffer_size;\nlet zc_intermed_cap = unsafe {\n    _zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size(\n        zc_buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets_zc, per_thread_temp_bytes,\n    )\n};\n\nlet logup_buffer_size = single_pk.other_data.logup_round0_buffer_size;\nlet logup_intermed_cap = unsafe {\n    _logup_r0_intermediates_buffer_size(\n        logup_buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets_logup, per_thread_temp_bytes,\n    )\n};\n```\n\n**Relationship to constraint degree:**\n- `num_cosets_zc = constraint_degree.saturating_sub(1)`\n- `num_cosets_logup = constraint_degree`\n- Intermediates scales linearly with constraint_degree\n\n---\n\n### **6. REMNANTS OF BATCHED ROUND 0 CODE**\n\n**Status:** Completely reverted from current HEAD. Batched Round 0 infrastructure was attempted but removed.\n\n#### **Reverted Commits:**\n1. **0c699f47** (Apr 13, 16:08): \"Batch Round 0 descriptor arrays: CUDA kernels, FFI, and Rust batch helpers (infrastructure)\"\n   - Reverted by **b617e156** (Apr 13)\n   - Added: `Round0ZcCtx`, `Round0LogupCtx` descriptor structs\n   - Added: `batched_zerocheck_r0_coset_parallel_kernel`, `batched_logup_r0_coset_parallel_kernel`\n   - 959 lines of code\n\n2. **bcb1c0d2** (Apr 13, 18:25): \"Batch Round 0 caller-routing: CUDA kernels, FFI, orchestration module\"\n   - Reverted by **73c8440c** (Apr 13)\n   - Re-introduced batched kernels with new `round0_batched.rs` module (#[inline(never)] orchestration)\n   - Added functions: `identify_batchable_airs()`, `batch_round0_small_airs()`, `merge_results()`\n   - 1356 lines added, introduced per-AIR memory budget filter (`MAX_INTERMEDIATES_PER_AIR`)\n   - 727 lines in dedicated `round0_batched.rs` module\n\n#### **Why Reverted:**\nThe autoopt-results history shows these were reverted after initial attempts:\n- **Apr 13-14**: Exploratory batch descriptors (dir: `2026-04-13-1600-batch-round0-descriptor-arrays`)\n- **Apr 13-14**: Batch caller routing (dir: `2026-04-13-1700-batch-round0-caller-routing`)\n- **Apr 13-14**: Interleaved work balancing replaced batching (commit **6b940845**)\n- **Apr 14**: Multi-stream stacked reduction became the strategy (commit **a2f5d2d9**, reverted at **8b7c70ab**)\n\n#### **What Survives:**\n- **No `round0_batched.rs` module** in current codebase\n- **No `Round0ZcCtx` or `Round0LogupCtx` structs** (only exist in MLE as `ZerocheckCtx`, `LogupCtx` for different purposes at lines 48, 62 in cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs)\n- **No batched Round 0 CUDA kernels** (only per-AIR single-AIR kernels remain)\n- **Per-AIR multi-threading** is the current strategy (as of commit **6b940845**, May 13)\n\n#### **Git History Search Results:**\n```\n21c878af Overlap logup combination precompute with Round 0 multi-stream evaluation (CURRENT)\n423044cb GPU-side Round 0 polynomial extraction via pre-computed transform matrices\n8b7c70ab Revert \"Multi-stream Stacked Reduction Round 0 sumcheck and PLE fold\"\na2f5d2d9 Multi-stream Stacked Reduction Round 0 sumcheck and PLE fold\ne6f614f2 Pre-allocate per-thread Round 0 GPU buffers with adaptive 95th-percentile threshold\n6b940845 Round 0 interleaved work balance: replace contiguous chunking with round-robin assignment\n73c8440c Revert \"Batch R