 kernels, FFI, and Rust batch helpers\n```\n\n---\n\n### **7. EXTRACTION KERNEL FLOW**\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/round0_extract.cu`\n\n#### **Zerocheck Extraction** (Lines 23-39)\n```cuda\n__global__ void round0_extract_zerocheck_kernel(\n    FpExt* __restrict__ d_out,\n    const FpExt* __restrict__ d_evals,        // Evaluation buffer from constraint kernel\n    const FpExt* __restrict__ d_transform,    // Pre-computed [output_size × input_size]\n    uint32_t input_size,                      // (d-1) * skip_domain\n    uint32_t output_size                      // sumcheck_round0_deg(l_skip, d) + 1\n) {\n    uint32_t i = threadIdx.x;\n    if (i >= output_size) return;\n    \n    // Each thread i computes one output coefficient via mat-vec multiply:\n    // output[i] = sum_j transform[i * input_size + j] * evals[j]\n    FpExt sum;\n    const FpExt* row = d_transform + static_cast<uint64_t>(i) * input_size;\n    for (uint32_t j = 0; j < input_size; j++) {\n        sum += row[j] * d_evals[j];\n    }\n    d_out[i] = sum;\n}\n```\n\n**Transformation pipeline** (computed on CPU in `compute_round0_extract_tables`, lines 138-209):\n1. Transpose evaluation array: `[NUM_COSETS][skip_domain]` → row-major\n2. Apply iDFT (inverse NTT) per coset\n3. Unshift by coset evaluation points (ω^c shifts)\n4. Lagrange interpolation at high-degree polynomial evaluation points\n5. Coefficient adjustment (for zerocheck only)\n\n**Writing to batch array:**\n- Called in `process_air_round0` (line 314) with offset `w.zc_batch_offset`\n- All zerocheck polynomials for present AIRs are written to contiguous device buffer\n- Single D2H transfer at end (mod.rs, line 1424)\n\n#### **Logup Extraction** (Lines 44-65)\n```cuda\n__global__ void round0_extract_logup_kernel(\n    FpExt* __restrict__ d_out_numer,\n    FpExt* __restrict__ d_out_denom,\n    const FracExt* __restrict__ d_evals,      // Numerator/denominator fractions\n    const FpExt* __restrict__ d_transform,\n    uint32_t input_size,                      // d * skip_domain\n    uint32_t output_size,                     // d * skip_domain\n    FpExt norm_factor                         // Scale for n_lift > 0\n) {\n    // Unpacks FracExt into numer (p) and denom (q),\n    // applies normalization to numer, then extracts via transformation\n}\n```\n\n**Result writing:**\n- Numerator to `w.numer_batch_offset` (mod.rs, line 374)\n- Denominator to `w.denom_batch_offset` (mod.rs, line 375)\n\n---\n\n### **8. KEY FILES AND LINE NUMBERS SUMMARY**\n\n| Component | File | Lines | Purpose |\n|-----------|------|-------|---------|\n| Main orchestration | `logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` | 244-389 | `process_air_round0()` per-AIR kernel dispatch |\n| Work item builder | `logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` | 1022-1152 | Prepare work items, extract tables, batch allocation |\n| Multi-stream dispatch | `logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` | 1204-1420 | Round-robin work distribution, thread spawning |\n| Round0 buffers | `logup_zerocheck/round0.rs` | 28-33 | `Round0ThreadBuffers` pre-allocation struct |\n| Extract tables | `logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` | 123-209 | `Round0ExtractTables` and `compute_round0_extract_tables()` |\n| Work item struct | `logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` | 212-242 | `Round0AirWorkItem<HS>` with buffer capacities |\n| Buffer size formulas | `cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/eval_config.cuh` | 61-106 | `intermediates_buffer_size()` and `temp_sums_buffer_size()` |\n| Zerocheck kernel | `cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/zerocheck_round0.cu` | 148-166 | `zerocheck_ntt_evaluate_constraints_kernel` |\n| Logup kernel | `cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/logup_round0.cu` | 161-178 | `logup_r0_ntt_eval_interactions_kernel` |\n| Zerocheck coset-parallel | `cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/zerocheck_round0.cu` | 250-350 | Coset-parallel variant (grid.y = num_cosets) |\n| Logup coset-parallel | `cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/logup_round0.cu` | 323-440 | Coset-parallel variant (grid.y = num_cosets) |\n| Extraction kernels | `cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/round0_extract.cu` | 23-99 | Zerocheck and logup polynomial extraction |\n| FFI declarations | `cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs` | 1-150 | Buffer size function declarations and descriptor structs (MLE, not Round 0) |\n| Key gen logup rules | `pkey.rs` | 113-150 | Pre-compute `logup_round0_buffer_size` at keygen |\n\n---\n\n### **SUMMARY**\n\nThe current Round 0 evaluation is **fully per-AIR**, processed via:\n\n1. **CPU orchestration** (sumcheck_uni_round0_polys) builds per-AIR work items with pre-computed buffer capacities\n2. **Multi-threaded dispatch** assigns work items to threads using round-robin balancing (after height-sorting)\n3. **Per-AIR sequential evaluation** calls `process_air_round0()` which:\n   - Evaluates zerocheck constraints on (constraint_degree-1) cosets\n   - Extracts zerocheck polynomial via GPU transformation matrix\n   - Evaluates logup interactions on constraint_degree cosets\n   - Extracts logup numerator/denominator polynomials via GPU transformation matrices\n4. **Single D2H copy** transfers all per-AIR results from device batch array to host\n5. **No batched infrastructure remains** - previous batched Round 0 attempts (commits 0c699f47, bcb1c0d2) were completely reverted\n\nThe intermediates buffer scales as **buffer_size × num_threads × num_cosets**, where buffer_size is per-AIR trace width × constraint degree, computed at keygen and capped at 95th percentile for multi-threaded pooling."}],"totalDurationMs":124763,"totalTokens":82619,"totalToolUseCount":43,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1273,"cache_read_input_tokens":74721,"output_tokens":6625,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1273},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":6625,"cache_read_input_tokens":74721,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1273,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":12