{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0112Cvf2U1y6bPoVicnnaSD5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Current Performance Summary\n\n| Component | APC 0 | APC 300 | Scaling | Ideal 2x | Gap |\n|-----------|-------|---------|---------|----------|-----|\n| STARK excl trace | 1783ms | 1114ms | 1.60x | 892ms | 222ms |\n| LogUp GKR | 703ms | 369ms | 1.90x | 352ms | 17ms |\n| Round 0 | 177ms | 180ms | 0.98x | 89ms | 91ms |\n| MLE Rounds | 118ms | 163ms | 0.72x | 59ms | 104ms |\n| Trace Commit | 476ms | 198ms | 2.40x | 238ms | -40ms |\n| Openings | 299ms | 201ms | 1.49x | 150ms | 51ms |\n\n## Optimization Ideas\n\n**Idea 1: Batched descriptor-array Round 0 for small AIRs**\n- Re-implement the previously attempted batched Round 0 kernels using caller-level routing. Batch all small AIRs (intermediates < L2 budget) into single descriptor-array kernel launches, while large AIRs continue with multi-stream per-AIR processing.\n- Expected: 60-100ms savings at APC 300, 0ms at APC 0\n- Probability: Medium (CUDA kernels were previously implemented; caller-routing solved Rust optimizer issue; OOM was unrelated)\n- Complexity: High\n\n**Idea 2: Batch precompute_logup_combinations kernel in MLE rounds**\n- Replace per-trace precompute kernel launches (~4400 per segment at APC 300) with batched descriptor-array launches (1 per round).\n- Expected: 40-50ms savings at APC 300, 7ms at APC 0\n- Probability: Medium-High (descriptor-array pattern well-established in MLE rounds)\n- Complexity: Moderate\n\n**Idea 3: GPU-accelerated Stacked Reduction polynomial reconstruction**\n- Move CPU NTT reconstruction (~36ms of 74ms Stacked Reduction) to GPU.\n- Expected: 25-30ms savings at both APC configs\n- Probability: Medium (complex NTT variant)\n- Complexity: Moderate\n\n**Idea 4: Fuse zerocheck + logup NTT in Round 0**\n- Share the NTT coset evaluation between zerocheck and logup kernels.\n- Expected: 15-30ms savings\n- Probability: Low-Medium (kernel fusion complex, shared memory limits)\n- Complexity: High\n\n**Idea 5: Increase Round 0 thread count to 12-16**\n- Simple parameter change.\n- Expected: 10-20ms savings\n- Probability: Medium (diminishing returns past 8)\n- Complexity: Simple\n\n## Ranking (expected_impact × probability / complexity)\n\n1. **Idea 2**: 45ms × 0.7 / moderate = best ratio - safe, meaningful, specifically helps APC 300\n2. **Idea 1**: 80ms × 0.5 / high = high impact but risky\n3. **Idea 5**: 15ms × 0.5 / simple = easy but small\n4. **Idea 3**: 28ms × 0.5 / moderate = moderate everything\n5. **Idea 4**: 22ms × 0.3 / high = poor ratio\n\nI'll select **Idea 2: Batch precompute_logup_combinations in MLE rounds**. It has the best risk/reward profile, specifically targets per-AIR overhead that scales poorly with APC count, and follows an established pattern (descriptor-array batching) that has succeeded repeatedly in this codebase.\n\nLet me verify the precompute kernel code before writing the plan."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3372,"cache_read_input_tokens":156981,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3372},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cd67acf5-7001-4f85-a6f5-23b121ad763a","uuid":"c130dcae-066f-4a78-b883-ce2b43625426"}
